# Life // Death, a split card (CR 709), pictured from both sides at once: one copy has been cast as Life, so every
# land Bot1 controls is a 1/1 creature that is still a land, and a second copy is still in hand, where the client
# draws the whole card — the name "Life // Death", the two halves' costs and text — and offers two ways to cast it,
# one per half.
#
# The position a player has to read: the card in hand is one card with two spells on it, and which one is being cast
# is a choice made at the moment of casting rather than something the card says by itself. The spent copy in the
# graveyard is the same card again (CR 709.4), not the half that was cast.

